## A trader's come to deal
Asa Larkin the meat-peddler, a peddler out of Ipswich, has come to you with meat — the makings of your stew, which the village has gone without. In his pack: 4 cuts of meat (the customary price is about 2). Weigh his asking prices against what you know of their prices — counter a dear ask or let it go rather than overpay; a bale bought above what it sells on for is coin lost. Buy what you need with pay_with_item (seller "Asa Larkin the meat-peddler", item "meat", the quantity, consume_now false, coins in amount or goods you carry in pay_items, your words in say).

Weigh what's in front of you — obligations and pressing needs come before idle matters. Choose one action, then call done() when nothing pressing remains.
